.\" Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), explicit ELF debug-section selection.
.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt DWARF_ELF_INIT_SECTION 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dwarf_elf_init_section
.Nd initialize a reader for one ELF debug information section
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libdwarf
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In libdwarf.h
.Ft int
.Fn dwarf_elf_init_section "Elf *elf" "int mode" "Dwarf_Unsigned section" "Dwarf_Handler errhand" "Dwarf_Ptr errarg" "Dwarf_Debug *dbg" "Dwarf_Error *error"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The function initializes a reader like
.Xr dwarf_elf_init 3 ,
including application of ELF relocations.
A nonzero
.Fa section
selects an ELF section index whose name is
.Dq .debug_info ,
.Dq .debug_info.dwo ,
.Dq .debug_types
or
.Dq .debug_types.dwo .
Other sections with these four names are excluded from the reader.
Shared abbreviation, string and other debug sections remain available.
The abbreviation, string, string-offset and line tables must match the
selected section's ordinary or
.Dq .dwo
namespace; tables from the other namespace are excluded.
Duplicate auxiliary debug section names are rejected as ambiguous.
Grouped private abbreviation tables are not selected automatically.
.Pp
Offsets returned by this reader are relative to the selected section.
Applications combining multiple readers must keep their offset namespaces
separate and resolve type signatures themselves.
The ELF descriptor and its data must remain alive until
.Xr dwarf_finish 3 .
.Pp
A zero section index is equivalent to
.Xr dwarf_elf_init 3
and retains its historical all-sections behavior.
Only
.Dv DW_DLC_READ
is supported.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The return values follow
.Xr dwarf_elf_init 3 .
An invalid index, a non-debug section, an unsupported mode or ambiguous
auxiliary sections produce
.Dv DW_DLV_ERROR
with
.Dv DW_DLE_ARGUMENT .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dwarf_elf_init 3 ,
.Xr dwarf_next_cu_header_d 3 ,
.Xr dwarf_object_init 3
